## 5. GLOBAL NAVIGATION

Create a minimal, persistent navigation system.

### Desktop behavior

- Place the logo at the left, navigation in the center where appropriate, and one high-value CTA at the right.
- Keep navigation labels short and immediately understandable.
- Use a restrained header height of approximately 48–64 px, subject to the design.
- Use a white or subtly translucent background where appropriate.
- Introduce a light backdrop blur only if it improves separation from scrolling content.
- Add a subtle bottom border or background change when the page scrolls.
- Maintain adequate contrast regardless of the content beneath the header.

### Mega-menu interaction

When a user hovers over or activates a primary navigation item:

- Reveal a clean, spacious mega-menu.
- Group links according to user intent rather than internal organizational structure.
- Use a soft background transition and restrained blur or dimming behind the menu.
- Animate opacity and vertical position over approximately 180–280 ms.
- Support keyboard focus, Escape to close, and click or tap to open.
- Prevent flickering when moving the pointer between trigger and menu.
- Close appropriately when focus or interaction leaves the menu.
- Respect touch-device behavior; do not depend on hover.

Do not add a mega-menu if a simpler navigation system is sufficient.

### Mobile navigation

- Use a compact header with a clear menu control.
- Open a full-screen or spacious overlay menu.
- Provide large, comfortable touch targets.
- Keep the close control obvious.
- Lock background scrolling only while the overlay is open.
- Restore focus correctly when the menu closes.
- Prevent accidental activation of underlying content.

